error[E0316]: `all_of` cannot be part of an overload set because it collects arguments with a `*` parameter
  --> tests/ui/macro_overload_errors.wid:35:17
   |
29 | macro def all_of(*names: Symbol) -> Code
   |           ------ declared here
...
35 | overload :many, :all_of, :from_text
   |                 ^^^^^^^ not allowed in an overload set
   = note: a call picks a member by the number and types of its arguments, which a `*` parameter leaves open
help: remove `:all_of` from the set and call it by its own name
   = see `wid explain E0316`

error[E0108]: statements must be inside a method
  --> tests/ui/macro_overload_errors.wid:38:1
   |
38 | pick "text"
   | ^^^^^^^^^^^ this call is outside any `def`
   = note: `from_text` is a method, not a macro; only a macro call can stand among declarations
help: move it into `def main … end`, which runs when the program starts
   = see `wid explain E0108`

error[E0316]: several members of `either` take (integer literal, integer literal)
  --> tests/ui/macro_overload_errors.wid:41:5
   |
41 |   p either(1, 2)
   |     ^^^^^^^^^^^^ `first_code` and `second_code` fit equally well
   = note: the members are `first_code(e: Code, n: Int)`, `second_code(n: Int, e: Code)`
help: call one member by name, like `first_code(…)`
   = see `wid explain E0316`

error[E0316]: no member of `pick` takes (Bool)
  --> tests/ui/macro_overload_errors.wid:42:5
   |
42 |   p pick(true)
   |     ^^^^^^^^^^ called with (Bool)
   = note: the members are `from_int(n: Int)`, `from_text(s: String)`
help: no conversion makes (Bool) fit a member: pass arguments of one member's parameter types, or call a member by name, like `from_int(…)`
   = see `wid explain E0316`

error[E0303]: overloaded calls take positional arguments
